Advanced time-domain, dispersion and PML validation (@em-time-numerics-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Understanding-FDTD-Schneider.lingua#r_3BTKKSTADJQXT1XD3S4WZVBMYM", #source "../sources/Notes-on-Perfectly-Matched-Layers-Johnson.lingua#r_0NSKFHQZEZSB48A279RTVFB8HM", #source "../sources/Meep-Methods-Manual.lingua#r_7V0TJSMDBGNHBD0MBTB94W8GRX", #source "../sources/Meep-Original-Paper.lingua#r_6VNPZYYD3SYGHFATA6VKQ5QD8K", #electromagnetism "../study/An-integrated-electromagnetic-system-investigation.lingua#r_1FQW2ASX2WCT3JRXKKP4NB4HSN") { r_3DN369CNVW889T4MG6CAAXJGCV
**Read:** [Understanding the Finite-Difference Time-Domain Method — John B. Schneider](../sources/Understanding-FDTD-Schneider.lingua#r_3BTKKSTADJQXT1XD3S4WZVBMYM), complete available book and substantial worked implementations; [Notes on Perfectly Matched Layers — Steven G. Johnson](../sources/Notes-on-Perfectly-Matched-Layers-Johnson.lingua#r_0NSKFHQZEZSB48A279RTVFB8HM), entire paper; [Meep — methods, tutorials, validation and licence](../sources/Meep-Methods-Manual.lingua#r_7V0TJSMDBGNHBD0MBTB94W8GRX), all applicable complete method sections and tutorials; [Meep — Oskooi and colleagues, 2010](../sources/Meep-Original-Paper.lingua#r_6VNPZYYD3SYGHFATA6VKQ5QD8K), entire authorized article.

Read the entire available [Understanding the Finite-Difference Time-Domain Method — John B. Schneider](../sources/Understanding-FDTD-Schneider.lingua#r_3BTKKSTADJQXT1XD3S4WZVBMYM) book, all of [Notes on Perfectly Matched Layers — Steven G. Johnson](../sources/Notes-on-Perfectly-Matched-Layers-Johnson.lingua#r_0NSKFHQZEZSB48A279RTVFB8HM), the complete applicable [Meep — methods, tutorials, validation and licence](../sources/Meep-Methods-Manual.lingua#r_7V0TJSMDBGNHBD0MBTB94W8GRX) method/tutorial material and an authorized full [Meep — Oskooi and colleagues, 2010](../sources/Meep-Original-Paper.lingua#r_6VNPZYYD3SYGHFATA6VKQ5QD8K) paper. Reconstruct a Yee update, its mode dispersion and stability condition before relying on a multidimensional implementation. The original periodic example gives an exact discrete starting benchmark.

Build a sequence of tests: uniform fields, an exact Fourier mode, a pulse in a homogeneous medium, an interface, a finite dielectric structure and a radiating/scattering case. Separate temporal/spatial error, geometry error, source normalization and open-boundary error. Include a dispersive material only after validating its auxiliary update and physical response.

Measure PML reflection against enlarged-domain and thickness/resolution limits, including a difficult evanescent or near-grazing case discussed by the primary paper. Compare frequency-domain energy flux with time-domain work and independently available analytical limits. Preserve exact software version and external input provenance. The report should show both a successful convergence result and a diagnosed failure; a stable animation or a solver's reputation cannot establish the claimed accuracy of a new electromagnetic observable.

**Continue:** [An integrated electromagnetic-system investigation](../study/An-integrated-electromagnetic-system-investigation.lingua#r_1FQW2ASX2WCT3JRXKKP4NB4HSN).

**Return:** [Electromagnetism — charge, fields, matter, waves and physical evidence](../Electromagnetism.lingua#r_5TJPESCTTNAKY66JH2QNQYN1PY).
